       }
      ],
      "text": "What these are:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " milestones most children (≥75%) are expected to reach by this visit age."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Social/emotional:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " follows rules or takes turns when playing games with other children; sings, dances, or acts for you; does simple chores at home, like matching socks or clearing the table after eating."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Language/communication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tells a story she heard or made up with at least 2 events, like a cat stuck in a tree and a firefighter saving it; answers simple questions about a book or story after you read or tell it to him; keeps a conversation going with >3 back-and-forth exchange; uses or recognizes simple rhymes (bat-cat, ball-tall)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cognitive:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " counts to 10; names some numbers between 1 and 5 when you point to them; uses words about time, like yesterday, tomorrow, morning, or night; pays attention for 5–10 min during activities, for example, during story time or making arts and crafts (screen time does not count); writes some letters in her name; names some letters when you point to them."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
